Package: kpqc
Type: Package
Title: Korean Post-Quantum Cryptography Algorithms
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Owen", "Suolfou", email = "osuolfou@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Copyright: see file COPYRIGHTS
Description: Provides synchronous interfaces to four algorithms for
    post-quantum cryptography: 'AIMer', a digital-signature algorithm based
    on symmetric primitives; 'HAETAE', a module-lattice-based
    digital-signature algorithm; and 'NTRU+' and 'SMAUG-T', lattice-based
    key-encapsulation algorithms. These algorithms were selected by the
    Korean Post-Quantum Cryptography competition. Native reference
    implementations are compiled into the package and use operating-system
    entropy for key generation, signing, and encapsulation.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/KpqC/kpqc-r
BugReports: https://github.com/KpqC/kpqc-r/issues
Depends: R (>= 3.6.0)
Encoding: UTF-8
SystemRequirements: C11
NeedsCompilation: yes
